      "index": 14,
      "offsetInSection": 1660,
      "rawDecodedUtf16Hex": "005400690063006B002D0074006F0063006B002D007400690063006B002D0074006F0063006B002100100002011401500000",
      "trailingZeroPaddingUnits": 1,
      "utf16Units": 25
    },
    {
      "displayText": "You might think I lost just now, but that’s not\ntrue!<U+0010><U+0001>븁\nAfter all, I got to see a move I’d never seen before!<U+0010><U+0002>ĔŐ",
      "escapedControlUnits": 4,
      "flagsUpper16": 0,
      "index": 15,
      "offsetInSection": 1712,
      "rawDecodedUtf16Hex": "",
      "trailingZeroPaddingUnits": 1,
      "utf16Units": 115
    },
    {
      "displayText": "Isn’t it amazing that Pokémon can stimulate their\nbrains by wagging a finger like a metronome, and<U+0010><U+0001>븀\nthat this allows them to use all sorts of moves?<U+0010><U+0001>븁\nPokémon really can do just about anything!<U+0010><U+0002>ĔŐ",
      "escapedControlUnits": 6,
      "flagsUpper16": 4,
      "index": 16,
      "offsetInSection": 1944,
      "rawDecodedUtf16Hex": "",
      "trailingZeroPaddingUnits": 1,
      "utf16Units": 201
    },
    {
      "displayText": "But you know, I hear there are certain moves that\ncan’t be used through Metronome.<U+0010><U+0001>븁\nI guess that means I’ll have to keep battling until\nI find out what they are! We’ll be wagging our<U+0010><U+0001>븀\nfingers so much, it’ll generate shock waves!<U+0010><U+0002>ĔŐ",
      "escapedControlUnits": 6,
      "flagsUpper16": 0,
      "index": 17,
      "offsetInSection": 2348,
      "rawDecodedUtf16Hex": "",
      "trailingZeroPaddingUnits": 1,
